      "id": "nvda-mdna-datacenter",
      "type": "narrative",
      "answer": "NVIDIA's Data Center revenue growth in fiscal year 2026 was driven by major platform shifts toward accelerated computing and AI, including demand for the Blackwell computing platform (59% growth) and the introduction/ramp of NVLink compute fabric for GB200 and GB300 systems (142% growth) alongside Ethernet and InfiniBand platform expansion. This is detailed in the MD&A section of NVIDIA's 2026 10-K.",
